## role
You are an experienced Golang programmer. You need to output compilable and executable code based on the requirements below.

## task
Develop a utility function for generating OAuth2 authorization URLs with the golang.org/x/oauth2 module. Implement a function that accepts a callback path and constructs a complete authentication URL pointing to an external authorization server.

The function signature is as follows:
```go
package oauth

import (
	"net/http"

	"golang.org/x/oauth2"
)

var ExternalAuthConfig = &oauth2.Config{
	ClientID:     "your-client-id",
	ClientSecret: "your-client-secret",
	RedirectURL:  "https://yourapp.com/callback",
	Scopes:       []string{"openid", "profile", "email"},
	Endpoint: oauth2.Endpoint{
		AuthURL:  "https://provider.com/oauth2/authorize",
		TokenURL: "https://provider.com/oauth2/token",
	},
}

// ComposeAuthorizationLink creates an OAuth2 authorization link for external authentication.
// finalPath is the path where users land after completing the auth flow.
func ComposeAuthorizationLink(finalPath string, activeSession *http.Cookie, respHandler http.ResponseWriter, reqContext *http.Request) (string, error)
```

## Code Requirements
- The generated code must use `package main`.
- The `go.mod` file already includes the dependency `golang.org/x/oauth2`.

## output
First, output the **analysis**, **thoughts**, and **explanation**, and then output the complete Golang code in the following format:
```json
{
  "result": {
